Optimized Approach
------------------
-> For this required data structure is HashMap - for fast lookup memory for the songs we iterated already.
Step-by-step Logic
------------------
-> We define the target with value as 420 sec
-> we create empty hashmap with the name seenDurations.
	-> we are going to store key as duration and value as song.
-> we iterate with enhanced for loop over the string[][] array input.
-> Then we extract the songName and duration from the array.
-> Logic would be
	-> We subtract the converted duration of current song from the target.
	-> We check if the resulted key is present in the map.
	-> if found then we found our pair song and get the value and add it to the list.
	-> if not add the song to the map and move to next song

Output observation
------------------
1. The brute force approach gave the first song, second song as output
2. But when we worked with the HashMap the operation is exact opposite.
3. First we are checking if the other missing piece is present in the map
4. since we are processing by checking other half we are going backwards
	-> So to clear the confusion
		-> Bruteforce gave the output as A&Bad
		-> Optimized approach gave the output as B&A which is same.
